{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Do not hold another referendum on the UK rejoining the European Union",
        "additional_details": "In 2016, the British people voted for the UK to leave the European Union. The UK formally left the EU in 2020. We believe that decision should be respected. We call on the UK Government not to hold another referendum on whether the UK should rejoin the European Union. Another referendum could be expensive, divisive and we believe would create uncertainty for businesses, workers and families. The Government should make clear that it has no plans to rejoin the EU during this Parliament.",
        "background": "The UK voted to leave the European Union in 2016 and formally left in 2020. We believe that decision should be respected. We call on the UK Government not to hold another referendum on whether the UK should rejoin the EU, to avoid further division, cost and uncertainty for businesses.",
